# HomeWorld Project Context — RETIRED (P4)

This rule was an `alwaysApply: true` project card. It is **retired**, not
deleted, so any surviving reference resolves to a pointer.

**Why:** it was a stale fork of `AGENTS.md`. Every section had a counterpart
that was already better maintained:

| Was here | Now lives in |
|---|---|
| Project purpose, UE 5.8, PC + Steam EA | `AGENTS.md` → MVP canon table + Lock |
| Tech stack, enabled plugins | `AGENTS.md` → Stack (enabled plugins) |
| Key Principles (programmatic-first, MCP-first, idempotency, automation) | `AGENTS.md` throughout; details in `00-core-principles.mdc` |
| Project Structure, Key Files | `AGENTS.md` → MVP canon table (`Docs/` vs `docs/`) |
| Conventions (naming, UE 5.8 sources, PowerShell `;`) | `AGENTS.md` → Code style |
| Onboarding Quick-Start (5 steps) | `AGENTS.md` → Dev environment setup (same 5 steps) |

It also carried three references to files that do not exist, all of which would
have sent an agent looking for a doc that is not in the repo:
`docs/TASKLIST.md`, `docs/MCP_SETUP.md` (real path `docs/Setup/MCP_SETUP.md`),
and `docs/PCG_BEST_PRACTICES.md` (real path `docs/PCG/PCG_BEST_PRACTICES.md`).

It was also the wrong place for a product fact: the "8-12h campaign + endgame"
target is signed MVP canon and belongs in `Docs/`, not in an agent rule.

## Do not

Do not restore this card or create a replacement "project context" rule.
`AGENTS.md` is the always-on surface. If project context is missing there, add
it to `AGENTS.md`, not to a new always-apply rule.
